# Real Garry's Mod backdoors, caught in the wild and published. This file records
# what the scanner manages against them.
#
# The samples are NOT stored in this repository. malicious_corpus.sh clones each
# source at the commit pinned below and verifies every file against the hashes
# listed here, so an upstream edit cannot silently change what is being tested.
# The clone pins core.autocrlf=false, so the hashes are of the bytes as stored
# rather than whatever the local platform would check out.
#
# A family is one backdoor. Its recorded severity is the best the scanner reaches
# on any of its files: the question is whether the thing would have been stopped,
# not whether every fragment looks alarming alone. Several families ship a
# deobfuscated copy made by the analyst next to the original; both are scanned.
#
# Not every family is expected to reach CRITICAL, and recording otherwise would be
# dishonest. A file whose entire content is a hook that blocks kicks is worth
# knowing about, but it is not a server takeover, and HIGH is the right answer.
# The floor counts only the families that do reach CRITICAL.
#
# One family is recorded as none, and that is a decision rather than a shortfall.
# The rules look for code that runs at runtime, fetches from somewhere, hides what
# it does, or digs itself in. A published addon whose author wired a prank into the
# chat handler does none of those: it is ordinary Lua doing something the server
# owner did not ask for. A rule that caught it would have to fire on the kind of
# code every gamemode is made of, and the false positives would cost more than the
# family is worth. Where a sample is missed for a reason worth fixing, it belongs
# in lua_patterns.test.txt as a case, not here as an excuse.
#
# Lowering any line here, or the floor, is a claim that the scanner got worse.
# Raising one is the point of the exercise.
#
# Deliberately not included: client-side cheat menus. They are malicious, but a
# server backdoor scanner is the wrong tool for them and counting them would
# misreport what it does.

# family-recall-floor 23

source bb2015       https://github.com/BannedGithub/Backdoor_Busting_2015 e6df2783cbac9ce95e53b0511aa68eb76358ee32
source kdrm         https://github.com/Maxime48/kdrm-gmod-backdoor f305627cdd
source kickblock    https://github.com/Bigmanting24/gmod-backdoor-test 10a53fc87b
source payloads     https://github.com/SeenKid/gmod_payloads 18ac925cb0
source scannerkill  https://github.com/YohSambre/gmod_antibackdoor_system_fucker 6a1693cae7
source cmdremove    https://github.com/YohSambre/gmod_nuc_fuck_rp_resetallmoney_command c22216d96a
source grobyware    https://github.com/shane7716/Gmod-Backdoor-Menu-Grobyware 881f1ef1fe

# bb2015 -- Labelled database of backdoors found on live servers in 2015 and 2016.
#   "gpwn" / "pwn" backdoor.
bb2015/BD001_gpwn_new                        critical
#   "Underdone" backdoor/DRM annoyance script.
bb2015/BD002_Underdone                       critical
#   ThirdPersonController backdoor / Server takeover
bb2015/BD004_ThirdPersonController           critical
#   Vorox Goodman backdoor / Server takeover
bb2015/BD005_Vorox_Goodman                   critical
#   Pon bootstrap backdoor / Server takeover
bb2015/BD006_Pon_Bootstrap                   critical
#   Next_level Bigpayload backdoor / Server takeover
bb2015/BD007_Next_Level_Bigpayload           critical
#   Demonic King Leesin Backdoors / Server takeovers
bb2015/BD008_Demonic_King                    critical
#   Hammerfist Hammerfall Backdoor
bb2015/BD009_Hammerfist_Hammerfall           critical
#   French weapon scripts annoyance
bb2015/BD010_French_Weapon_Scripts           critical
#   Truly idiotic backdoor
bb2015/BD011_IdiotBackdoor                   critical
#   Another crappy one
bb2015/BD012_DoorHandler                     critical
#   Spams the chat and kills players when certain phrases are spoken in the ch
#   38 lines of plain Lua: a chat hook that prints and kills on a catchphrase.
#   No execution, no fetch, no obfuscation, nothing to persist. Out of scope on
#   purpose, see the note at the top.
bb2015/BD013_CPT_Base                        none
#   Various files, part of the same addon I think.
bb2015/BD014_Obfuscated_hud                  critical
#   Adds concommand "backdoor_ttt" to set the user's group to "superadmin"
bb2015/BD015_CW2_non_original                critical
#   Adds concommand "_sv" to RunString any lua code passed to it on the server
bb2015/BD016_GCap                            critical
#   Adds concommand "VIA" to set STEAM_0:1:56102047 as admin.
bb2015/BD017_Crash                           critical
#   Adds concommand "mememachine" to run remote lua on the server, for the fol
bb2015/BD018_AfterShock_Gaming               critical
#   "HTX" or "Hostile Takeover Exploit" backdoor. Includes client and server p
bb2015/BD019_HTX_Hostile_Takeover_Exploit    critical
#   Dumbass http.Fetch RunString backdoor
bb2015/BD020_Dumb                            critical
#   ShittyScripts backdoor (clientside)
bb2015/BD021_ShittyScripts                   critical

# kdrm -- Screen capture and player enumeration, 2025.
kdrm                                         critical

# kickblock -- Blocks the kick and ban events so the operator cannot be removed, 2025.
kickblock                                    high

# payloads -- Three backdoor payloads, 2023.
payloads                                     critical

# scannerkill -- Registers the console commands of six known scanners so their scans do nothing, 2024.
scannerkill                                  critical

# cmdremove -- Removes an admin console command, 2024.
cmdremove                                    high

# grobyware -- Decrypted backdoor control menu, 2019.
grobyware                                    critical

